Theorem RL-29: backend-neutral fresh-self-allocation fact derivation

  Preconditions:
    - RL-29 governs a backend-neutral AIMS fact. The final realization owner
      freezes it once from IC-4; executable backends transport and project it
      without re-running return-provenance analysis.
    - IC-4 carries returns_fresh_self_alloc separately from uniqueness and
      preserves_freshness. The stronger field is true only when every return
      path yields fresh storage with no upstream alias, directly or through a
      callee carrying the same path-universal proof.
    - A parameter passthrough and a result that may take over consumed input
      storage both set returns_fresh_self_alloc = false, even when freshness is
      otherwise preserved.
    - LLVM return noalias is a target projection after ABI selection. It is
      emitted only for a proven fact represented as a direct pointer.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per the canonical
      proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01 Realization.proof
      obligation.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-4 ReturnContract.returns_fresh_self_alloc; VF-2 (c)
      validates neutral fact derivation, while backend verification validates
      projection fidelity.

  Soundness property:
    Forall function return contracts C:

      (P1) Neutral decision:
           freshSelfAllocationFact(C.returns_fresh_self_alloc) = proven iff
           C.returns_fresh_self_alloc = true; otherwise notProven.

      (P2) Passthrough negative witness: caller-owned parameter storage is
           notProven and cannot receive target noalias.

      (P3) Consumed-storage negative witness: a result that may reuse consumed
           operand storage is notProven and cannot receive target noalias.

      (P4) Projection separation: LLVM maps proven + direct-pointer ABI to
           return noalias. notProven or a non-pointer/non-direct ABI omits it.
           LLVM spelling does not participate in P1.

    RL-29 exports one neutral return-provenance fact that every executable
    backend may project under its own ABI constraints.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the refinement engine via definitional rewriting
    of the IC-4 path-universal fact, followed by a separate LLVM
    projection-fidelity check.

    Part (P1/P2/P3) - neutral-fact grid:
      fresh_self_alloc_direct_pointer_noalias -> proven
      parameter_passthrough_not_proven -> notProven
      consumed_storage_not_proven -> notProven
      fresh_self_alloc_non_pointer_abi_omits_noalias -> proven
      Coverage gate: 4 derivations.

    Part (P4) - target corollary:
      proven + direct pointer -> LLVM return noalias
      notProven -> omitted
      proven + non-pointer/non-direct ABI -> omitted
      Negative-direction witness: consumed or forwarded storage must produce
      notProven + omitted.

    Engines dispatched:
      refinement (PRIMARY -
        section_08::verify_rl29_neutral_fresh_self_allocation; neutral IC-4
        return-provenance refinement followed by separate LLVM fidelity;
        emits Fail on an overclaiming fact or projection)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 refinement engine discharges RL-29 via a 4-row backend-neutral fresh-self-allocation grid gated solely on IC-4 returns_fresh_self_alloc, with passthrough and consumed-storage negative witnesses, then checks the separate LLVM fidelity corollary (proven direct pointer -> return noalias; all other cases -> omitted)
